fields.value:
 * Has the following targeting functionalities:
** {{Symbol|Target|AreaAlt}} {{to}} [[File:Dota2 Cast Range to AoE Visualization icon-5-1.png|84px]][[File:Dota2 Cast Range to AoE Visualization icon-5-2.png|84px]]
*** Can affect enemy units at max {{Symbol|bonus cas}} {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#expr:{{#var:Black Hole cast range}}+{{#var:Black Hole value2}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:{{#var:Black Hole cast range}}+{{#var:Black Hole type1 value1 agh}}}}|agh}})-distance away with the [[cast range]] and [[effect radius]].
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}} {{Symbol|Vision|Ground}}
**** Grants a 4-second {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} 800-radius {{M|caster vision}} at the area-targeted location upon cast.
***** The vision component is independent of the channeling component.
*** {{Symbol|Channeling|t}} {{Symbol|Aura}}
**** Creates two negative [[aura]]s that lasts as long as the {{M|channeling}} duration at the area-targeted location.
** {{Symbol|Target|Portrait}}
*** Considers [[portrait-casting]] as a {{Symbol|Target|Ground}} ground-targeted cast, and centers the radius around Enigma.

* The ability has two main components:
** {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** Does not affect the following units:
**** {{M|Buildings}}
**** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
*** Affects the following units:
**** {{M|Couriers}}
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|21px|1]] [[File:Dota2 Enigma Black Hole Visualized (Inner) icon.png|84px|Inner Radius]] {{to}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|enigma_black_hole_pull}}
*** The inner radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-r.png|21px|R]] applies the following ability effects to the debuff-affected enemy units:
**** {{Symbol|Forced Movement}}
***** Applies a {{M|disabling}} forced movement that pulls affected units to the center of the {{Symbol|Target|AreaAlt}} area-targeted location.
****** Can pull over {{M|impassable terrain}}.
****** Does not destroy {{M|trees}}.
***** Has the highest priority over other [[forced movement]] sources.
**** {{M|Leash}}
**** {{M|Silence}}
**** {{M|Stun}}
**** Deals {{M|pure}} {{M|spell damage}} + {{ValueColor||enemy max health as damage|agh}} in 1-second intervals, starting 1 second upon debuff application.
***** {{cf|aghnotes}} The additional spell damage is added to the base damage per second as a single damage instance in the {{M|combat log}}.
*** Affected units within inner radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-r.png|21px|R]] can be pulled out by various sources, except the following sources:
**** {{I|Force Staff}}-based items.
**** {{A|Earth Spirit|Geomagnetic Grip}}
**** {{A|Marci|Dispose}}
**** {{A|Tusk|Snowball}}
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|21px|2]] [[File:Dota2 Enigma Black Hole Visualized (Outer) icon.png|84px|Inner Radius]] {{to}} {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|enigma_black_hole_pull_scepter}}
*** The outer ring [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] applies the following ability effects to the debuff-affected enemy units:
**** {{Symbol|Forced Movement}}
***** Applies a non-disabling forced movement that pulls affected units to inner radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-r.png|21px|R]] within {{ValueColor||{{#var:Black Hole type1 value1 agh}}|agh}} radius.
****** Grants all affected enemy units {{M|phase movement}}.
****** Can pull over {{M|impassable terrain}}.
****** Affects the {{A|Monkey King|Tree Dance}} unit, but does not unperch it.
**** Does not affect the following enemy units:
***** While affected by other disabling forced movement sources.
***** While affected by {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|enigma_black_hole_pull}} within inner radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-r.png|21px|R]] .
**** {{cf|aghnotes}} The ability range indicator does not indicate the outer ring [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] .

